Fix inline source positions (columns and end lines) on continuation lines.

cmark-gfm strips leading indentation / blockquote markers from each line when
building a block's content buffer, but the inline parser applies only the
first line's offset to every line. As a result, inline nodes (code spans,
text, raw HTML) on indented continuation lines report columns that are short by
the stripped indentation. This records the stripped visual column of each
content line (blocks.c) and corrects the inline column offset per line
(inlines.c), storing the data on the node (node.h/node.c).

Reported upstream / to be submitted to github/cmark-gfm.

